The total weight of fruit is $84 \text{ (apples)} + 63 \text{ (oranges)} = 147$ ounces. She buys 3 full bags with an equal weight in each. Therefore, the capacity of each bag is $147 \div 3 = 49$ ounces. Alternatively, per bag she puts $21 \div 3 = 7$ pairs of fruits. Each pair weighs $4+3=7$ ounces. So each bag holds $7 \times 7 = 49$ ounces.

